This directory contains a Rust port of Future Crew's Panic, written by reverse
engineering the original and testing against its machine code. It is not a
clean-room implementation and has not been cleared for public release.

The repository's MIT License does not apply to this directory or to the import
and unpacking scripts tools/import_panic.py and tools/unpack_panic.py. No
licence over Future Crew material is granted. Whether the port can be freely
redistributed is still under review.

Original assets, unpacked executables and binary test fixtures are not included.
You must supply or generate them locally, under the terms of the original
release. Dependencies are fetched by Cargo, not bundled here, and remain under
their own licences.

Third-party code: the ray / rounded box intersection in src/hd/scroller.wgsl
(rounded_box() and the box normal in bump_hit()) is adapted from Inigo
Quilez's "Rounded Box - intersection", https://www.shadertoy.com/view/WlSXRW.
The same code appears in https://iquilezles.org/articles/intersectors/, which
states no licence itself; the MIT License below is the notice at the head of
that shader. It is Quilez's licence for his code. It doesn't extend to the
changes made here or to the rest of this directory, whose status is described
above. The notice is repeated next to the code.

